TzD (task #42): virtnet_rx_mode_work steps over the unicast list in bytes.
The multicast half of the MAC filter buffer starts at
&mac_data->macs[uc_count][0], the address of one 6-byte row, and the
code then writes the count and the multicast rows through it: past
that row (undefined in C; TzD bounds the row and traps).  Count from
the start of macs[] in bytes instead: the bounds of the whole buffer.
--- a/drivers/net/virtio_net.c	2026-11-13 20:47:07.849648844 +0900
+++ b/drivers/net/virtio_net.c	2026-11-13 20:47:07.865592645 +0900
@@ -3663,7 +3663,7 @@
 		   sizeof(mac_data->entries) + (uc_count * ETH_ALEN));
 
 	/* multicast list and count fill the end */
-	mac_data = (void *)&mac_data->macs[uc_count][0];
+	mac_data = (void *)((u8 *)mac_data->macs + uc_count * ETH_ALEN);
 
 	mac_data->entries = cpu_to_virtio32(vi->vdev, mc_count);
 	i = 0;
